WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.040
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Thank you very much for that.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.930
I am happy to take any questions, comments
on that report.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.450
If not, may I then turn to the Chief Executive's
report?

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.369
Simon, over to you.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:21.759
&gt;&gt;Simon Stevens: Thank you, Malcolm.

00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:25.390
You used the phrase 'choppy waters'; I was
going to say it has been a complex and intense

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.350
period since our last board meeting, but I
think choppy waters, if not white waters,

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:33.150
probably better catches it: obviously the
national stuff but also a lot of things the

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:37.360
NHS has been having to get to grips with as
well.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.140
Obviously, we have had the Brexit referendum
vote since last time, and so we are setting

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:50.480
up an NHS Brexit unit in NHS England to ensure
that, as the negotiations on the terms of

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.360
Brexit take shape, the NHS's interests are
properly represented there.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.890
We take account of both any opportunities
that might present, but also ensure that on

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:08.800
things like protecting the ability of the
NHS to continue to benefit from our international

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.470
employees, our employees from the European
Union, that is in hand; that we make smart

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:19.490
decisions about medicines licensing and the
life sciences industry in this new world;

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:24.150
we look at whether there are opportunities
for more flexible insurance arrangements;

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:32.030
and we ensure that as we, quote, 'take back
control' on things like public health measures

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.860
and regulations, that is an opportunity used
to enhance the work that we would want to

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:41.830
see on obesity and other public health threats.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:50.920
Secondly, the widely noted 'reset moment',
so called, occurred last Thursday, when we

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.860
and NHS Improvement published a set of actions
that will be taken across the NHS this year

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.200
to ensure that the National Health Service
lives within the funding that parliament has

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.610
allocated us for 2016/17.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:11.530
As part of that, as we previously discussed,
we have allocated the potential of £1.8 billion

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:19.530
to NHS trusts linked to trust specific improvement
trajectories that Matthew, I think, will talk

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:28.661
a bit about in his performance report, which
replaced the fines regime for this year: control

00:02:28.661 --> 00:02:35.780
totals for individual trusts and CCGs, with
step in action by ourselves for those CCGs

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.730
that have been struggling against the key
goals that they have been set and as measured

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:49.420
in the 2016/17 CCG assessment framework, the
results of which we published as part of the

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.920
reset last Thursday.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:56.120
Then various other financial controls layered
into the system, including much tighter oversight

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:02.870
and controls on the use of interim managers
in CCGs and CSUs to bring those costs down

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.430
as well.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:13.010
Thirdly, in addition to Brexit and the NHS
reset, we have collectively been using July

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:19.640
for intense discussions, face to face, with
most local NHS and local government leaders

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:24.120
across the country on how their service and
transformation plans are shaping up.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.560
These, as you recall, are their local implementation
plans for the Five Year Forward View; what

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:36.340
the Five Year Forward View will mean in Lincolnshire
or Leicestershire or Lancashire.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.791
Progress has been really very substantial,
actually, since we last had these face to

00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:43.830
face conversations two months ago.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:50.850
It is fair to say that the size of the challenge
and the degree to which people have collectively

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:57.790
mobilised was at different places when this
process got kicked off, but most people have

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.030
moved a very long way in a short period of
time.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:08.630
We are aiming to have well worked up financial
propositions in September, and then to be

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:14.690
able to agree most of the STPs by the end
of October.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:20.289
That, in turn, links to the fourth point,
which is that, in response to requests from

00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:25.460
across the front line of the NHS, we are bringing
forward the annual contracting round, making

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:31.490
it a two year job lot, so 2017/18 and 2018/19
combined.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:37.020
The aim is to have that wrapped up between
October and December, so that people have

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.900
figured out how they want to divvy the money
up locally, and can get on with the much more

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:48.820
profound job of actually redesigning and improving
services and care from January onwards.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:55.520
The specifics of that will be published in
part through the tariff engagement document,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.640
so called, which we will be getting out in
the course of week.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:05.480
Without spoiling all the fun, that will aim
to ensure stability and predictability in

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:09.820
what the tariff regime looks like for next
year.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:18.070
We will, as previously signalled, be proposing
moving over to a more specific way of referencing

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:24.370
tracking costs, through the so called HRG4
plus currency, better reflecting the costs

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.070
of more complex care.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:32.060
We will be proposing adding specialised service
top up payments that have been worked on intensively

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:37.880
with the providers of tertiary specialised
services, particularly for cancer, cardiac

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.070
and respiratory services.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:45.940
To the extent these improvements in the accuracy
mean volatility in the reimbursements for

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:51.750
individual providers, we are going to cap
that at no more than 0.5% a year, with consultation

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.710
proposed on how we do that.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:06:00.221
We are also not proposing introducing a marginal
rate for specialised services in 2017/18,

00:06:00.221 --> 00:06:07.919
or indeed 2018/19, and we will be promulgating,
in due course, a national option for people

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:14.770
to use an alternative to click of the turnstile
counting on their emergency volumes, if that

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.990
is what they want to do.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:21.780
So we think this goes with the grain of what
people are looking for in terms of tariff.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:28.220
At the same time, in September we will be
publishing proposals on CQUIN, the national

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.960
standard contract, the business rules, so
that really people have predictability as

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.050
to what the next couple of years will look
like, they can get that out of the way and

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:39.479
then, as I say, get on with the more fundamental
task of implementing the Forward View locally,

00:06:39.479 --> 00:06:44.100
through their STPs.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.460
The last point I should just note, Malcolm,
is that since last time we have continued

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:53.680
to make good on our commitment that, for NHS
England, this year would be a year of a shift

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.930
of focus from strategy to implementation.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.930
We have the blueprints we know we need on
cancer and mental health and learning disabilities

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:05.340
and urgent emergency care; it is sleeves rolled
up - it is indeed, very literally, sleeves

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.630
rolled up - focusing on the implementation.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:15.150
So we have published the implementation detail
on mental health - Claire Murdoch, Tim Kendall

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:21.080
- the most granular description of where the
money is coming from, where the extra workforce

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:26.350
is going to be trained, how we will deliver
the expanded services that we have seen at

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:30.610
any point in the history of mental health
services in this country, and we will be doing

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:33.050
the same on the other areas as well.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.680
Arvind today, later in this meeting, we will
be talking about some of the immediate steps

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:42.570
we are taking on support for general practice,
the urgent support that GPs need as well.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:50.620
So I think we are sort of going all guns blazing
against a backdrop of complexity and intense

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:55.550
scrutiny, not just of the NHS but the entire
public service.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.470
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Great, well thank you very
much for the report.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:02.620
Comments, questions from members of the board?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:09.580
No; I think they are dead impressed, and I
think many of the issues you have raised we

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:10.639
are also going to be developing

